          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best cordless drill</strong> is the one matched to what you actually build — a strong, brushless 18V drill/driver for general work, a compact 12V for tight spaces, a dedicated hammer drill if masonry is a regular job, and a drill and impact driver combo if you want one purchase that covers nearly everything. For most buyers, the <strong class="text-white">Milwaukee M18 FUEL Drill/Driver</strong> delivers the strongest all-around combination of torque and durability. For a lighter, kit-priced alternative, the <strong class="text-white">DeWalt 20V MAX XR</strong> is our top pick. And for masonry work, the <strong class="text-white">Milwaukee M18 FUEL Hammer Drill</strong> has no real substitute.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
